 "id": "homophones",
 "el": "Ομόηχες λέξεις",
 "title": "Same sound, different spelling",
 "level": "A2–C1",
 "intro": [
  "Greek has five ways to write the sound *i* (ι, η, υ, ει, οι) and two each for *o* (ο, ω) and *e* (ε, αι). Words that sound the same are told apart only in writing. You will hear them in dictation and have to spell them in the writing paper, so learn each with a short phrase."
 ],
